{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Celebrating Christmas"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Flashback"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 18}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le18ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present Perfect Tense versus The Simple Past Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a finished action or event that is connected to the present in some way.</p> You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event <span class=\"strong\">not</span> connected to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart about how to form the Present Perfect tense:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">have/has</span> + <span class=\"strong\">the past participle</span> of the verb in Present Perfect sentences."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past tense form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past participle form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"see\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"saw\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"seen\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I've never seen ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"get\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"got\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"gotten/got\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I haven't got ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"skate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"skated\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"skated\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I haven't skated ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"finish\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"finished\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"finished\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When we've finished ...\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I haven't skated for a long time."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I haven't got any skates."}, {"type": "example", "content": "When we've finished we can come back here."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Did someone build a rink in their backyard? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "It wasn't as crowded."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Used to and Would to Talk About Past Habits"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Used to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">would</span> are both used to talk about actions that happened in the past. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use <span class=\"italic\">used to</span> to express a past  action or state that is no longer happening. It uses -ed to show past tense.</p>  For example: She used to ride her bike everyday.</br>  (Before, she rode her bike everyday, but now she doesn't ride everyday.)</p>  My cousins used to play in the snow all day long. </br> (Before, they played in the snow all day long, but now they don't play in the snow.)</p>  We can use <span class=\"italic\">would </span>  to express repeated past actions and past routines.</p>  "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I used to go to the swimming pool everyday. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I don't do this anymore.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She would get a large coffee after lunch.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It was my habit in the past.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I used to play hockey with the other kids a lot. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We would play on the street if it wasn't cold enough to make ice."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They used to make ice?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We would play until we were too cold to continue."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "backyard"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an area behind a house "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sometimes we had a rink in our backyard. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about Christmas activities."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hockey"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a game played on ice with sticks and a puck "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We would play hockey all day long. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to skate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to use skates to move on ice"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We skated at the Boston Common. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to build"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to construct; to make "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We built a skating rink in our backyard."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob09aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "clever"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "intelligent "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Skating was a clever way to keep the kids active at Christmas. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob09aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to reheat "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to heat again after it is cold."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can reheat the leftovers for dinner."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob09aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of 6 activities you used to do as a child."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write sentences saying where you would do these activities."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include who you used to go with and when you used to do the activities."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your sentences to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I make a list of activities I did as a child."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write sentences for each activity."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I say where and when I used to do the activities."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I say who used to go with."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my sentences aloud."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about celebrations, customs, and traditions about food."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can discuss experiences I've had or haven't had."}